    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49144" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĭŏpas</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τριόπας,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of
			Thessaly</i>, <i>the father of Erisichthon</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg.
				Astr. 2, 14</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĭŏpēïus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>the son of
				Triopas</i>, i. e. <i>Erisichthon</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				751</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trĭŏpēïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				granddaughter of Triopas and daughter of Erisichthon</i>, i. e.
				<i>Mestra</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				872</span></i>.</div>
